From 0f2b0817933389820805a1ba8c9669f5bb75390d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:54:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 219/219] docs: record why d8f5dad4's blend-layer gate never
 gated anything in the engine

CryFX does not evaluate `#if <a macro the shader #defines>`. The body is emitted whatever the
value is, and only platform symbols (ORBIS, DURANGO, FEATURE_SVO_GI) work in a `#if` at all.

Proved against the engine's own dump of the failing translation unit, obtained with
r_ShadersDebug 1 on the mask 0x4000400002841020: the file contains the `%BLENDLAYER` block in
full, with no `#if` and no trace of RT_HIT_BLEND_LAYER, even though the source read

    #define RT_HIT_BLEND_LAYER 0
    #if RT_HIT_BLEND_LAYER  ...  #endif

So the stopgap gated nothing in the engine, the crash it was written to avoid never went away,
and the harness - whose translation unit is preprocessed by fxc, where the `#if` works as
written - called the same commit green. That divergence is the whole reason the two disagreed.

Decision 11 removes the construct along with the block, so this is a comment and a rule, not a
fix: cryfx_lint.py gained rule R8 for it (outside git, in scene-notes/rt/tools/).

The same dump also confirms the crash itself: compiled verbatim it fails with
"internal error: compilation aborted unexpectedly" on both compiler builds, and the ONE line
change already made in 51009ff4 - putting RT_RecordTC's argument in a named local - makes the
engine's own file compile (2442 instruction slots). With decision 11 applied to that same file
the trace pass is 2035 slots, and it still compiles with 24 further blend-block-sized layers
added on top.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SCUvWGLCsqzm3VNMzp4uiS
---
 Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi
index 227073ce..3c25f82c 100644
--- a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi
+++ b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi
@@ -109,6 +109,18 @@ float4 SVO_RTParams1;
 //
 // The rule that follows: ANYTHING THAT ONLY NEEDS THE WINNING TRIANGLE GOES IN ShadePS. The
 // traversal may only grow if the new work decides WHICH triangle wins.
+//
+// CRYFX DOES NOT EVALUATE "#if <a macro this file #defines>". The body is emitted whatever the
+// value is. The stopgap this block replaces was written as
+//     #define RT_HIT_BLEND_LAYER 0
+//     #if RT_HIT_BLEND_LAYER  ...  #endif
+// and the engine's own dump of the failing translation unit (r_ShadersDebug 1, 2026-09-14,
+// scene-notes/rt/tools/rtharness2/dumps/) contains the blend layer IN FULL, with no #if and no
+// trace of the macro - so that commit gated nothing in the engine and the crash below never
+// went away, while the harness, whose translation unit is preprocessed by fxc where the #if
+// works as written, reported it green. PLATFORM macros (ORBIS, DURANGO, FEATURE_SVO_GI) are
+// the parser's own symbols and do work. For anything else there is no compile-time switch in
+// CryFX: use a %-flag, or delete the code. cryfx_lint.py rule R8 now catches this.
 
 #define VOX_RT_MAX_BOUNCES                 (SVO_RTParams0.x)
 #define VOX_RT_GLOSS_SCALE                 (SVO_RTParams0.y)
